---
export const theme = {
  id: "summer-rainforest",
  displayName: "Summer rainforest + snorkeling",
  notchLabel: "Rainforest",
  status: "Reference",
  notchColor: "#e6f2ea",
  slug: "summer-rainforest-snorkeling",
  summary: "Context-specific criteria for warm rainforest travel with snorkeling.",
};

const siteTitle = `Theme: ${theme.displayName} – La Familia`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{siteTitle}</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        --text: #1f2933;
        --muted: #5b6570;
        --border: #d7dce1;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --accent: #2f5d7c;
        --background: #f6f7f9;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: "Inter", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background: var(--background);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 960px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 64px 24px 104px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 32px;
      }

      h1,
      h2 {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      p {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .section {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 28px 32px;
      }

      .subtitle {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        max-width: 720px;
      }

      .note {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="section">
        <h1>Theme: {theme.displayName}</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Planning context focused on warm rainforest settings with reliable snorkeling access and
          a calm, recovery-friendly pace.
        </p>
        <p class="note">This theme is scoped to June–July travel windows.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Theme constraints</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Trip timing is limited to June–July and must align with school break windows.</li>
          <li>Humidity and heat need to be tolerable for extended outdoor time.</li>
          <li>Rainfall patterns should still allow daily outdoor activity and water access.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Weather + snorkeling reliability</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Snorkeling quality must be dependable during the travel window.</li>
          <li>Prefer clear-water conditions with safe, low-current access from shore or short boat
            rides.</li>
          <li>Daily rain should be intermittent rather than continuous, with morning or mid-day water
            windows.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Logistics and routing</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Limit internal transfers; prioritize one primary base with optional day trips.</li>
          <li>Accommodations should be close to water access without long daily commutes.</li>
          <li>Ground transport should be predictable and low-stress for a family group.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Nice-to-have additions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Optional Singapore stopover for transit recovery and food access.</li>
          <li>Light cultural activities that do not replace water-focused days.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
